    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n1. **Governance test issue**: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` while keeping the default export intact.\n\n2. **Eval test issue**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving references as its second parameter (from `runEvaluations` calling it with `metric(outs, refs)`), but it was treating those references as `bannedTerms`. I updated the function signature to accept `references` as an explicit parameter and use the default `bannedTerms` instead, making it consistent with how `exactMatchMetric` and `lengthVarianceMetric` handle the references parameter.\n\nAll 28 tests in the frai-core suite are now passing.",
